About the role
MJ Consultants Limited is seeking a reliable, organised and technically capable Administration Officer (IT Support) to support the smooth day-to-day running of our office and technology environment.
This role is ideal for a proactive individual who enjoys balancing administrative coordination with practical IT support. You will be responsible for office administration, record management, procurement, staff support, and the maintenance of basic IT systems, hardware, software, and network services.
Key Responsibilities:
Administration
Manage daily office operations, filing, correspondence, records, and data entry;
Handle incoming calls, emails, visitors, and general enquiries professionally;
Organise company events, including Christmas parties, annual dinners, team-building activities, and staff celebrations;
Coordinate event venues, catering, invitations, transport, and schedules;
Perform other duties or ad hoc projects as assigned.
IT Support
Provide first-line IT support to employees;
Monitor and maintain office hardware and software applications;
Maintain an up-to-date inventory of IT assets.
>
Requirements:
Higher Diploma or above in Business Administration, Information Technology, or a related discipline;
Minimum 1-year working experience;
Fresh graduates are welcome to apply;
Good command of written and spoken English and Chinese;
Organised, responsible, detail-oriented, and able to handle multiple tasks;
A positive attitude with good communication and interpersonal skills;
Eligibility to work in Hong Kong is required. Applications from eligible non-local graduates under the Immigration Arrangements for Non-local Graduates (IANG) are welcome.
>
Benefits Including:
5-day Work
Medical Insurance
Annual Leave
Birthday Leave
Marriage Leave
Education Subsidy
Performance Bonus
We offer a working environment that fosters continuous learning and supports personal growth, career development and advancement. Interested parties please send CV with expected salary via ••••@mjcl.com.hk or to MJ Group, 2501-5, Laws Commercial Plaza, 788 Cheung Sha Wan Road, Kowloon, Hong Kong or click "APPLY NOW ". For more company details, please view our company webpage www.mjcl.com.hk.
The personal data collected will be treated with strict confidence and used for recruitment-related purposes only.

Job Responsibility:
Responsible for overall IT infrastructure management, security & services from design, configuration, implementation, operation to maintenance;
Evaluate organization outcomes; identify and resolve problems related to network infrastructure, hardware components, operating systems;
Implement disaster recovery and back-up procedures and information security and control structures;
Understand the current data management system and provide streamline solution for system upgrade and optimization.
Help to establish and maintain ISO27001 policies and procedures for Infrastructure and Operations.
Provide helpdesk support services and training to the end user.
Negotiate with external vendors and contractors for infrastructure-specific products and services.
>
Knowledge and Requirements:
High Diploma or above in a computer-related subject;
Minimum 5-year of experience in IT infrastructure planning, implementation, operation;
Working experience in WAN/LAN, Firewalls, DNS, DHCP, SAN, NAS Storage and TCP/IP.
Hands-on experience with Windows Servers, Linux, Virtualization technologies (VMWare, Docker), Databases (Oracle, MSsql, Mysql), Azure and AWS Cloud platform.
Knowledge in programming languages such as java, python, php.
Have experiences in handling IT infrastructure projects with internal teams and external vendors or partners;
Strong problem solving, root cause analysis techniques, and able to work independently.
Good command of both written and spoken English and Chinese
Holder of MCSE, CISSP is a plus

